# gcc stays at the installed 16.2.0 (user 2026-11-10). Until then the upgrade was
# blocked by a package.provided entry (sys-devel/gcc-16.2.1_p20260926), which made
# every world update warn "listed in package.provided ... pulled in by selected,
# system". A mask is the honest tool: the installed version stays visible and
# rebuildable, only newer ones (16.2.1_p* snapshots, 17.x) are out. The host and
# the hard images share one gcc slot and one binpkg lineage, so this file is the
# same on both sides. Lift deliberately, never by accident: a gcc bump means
# rebuilding the toolchain-sensitive stack (CUDA host compiler cap, kmods).
>sys-devel/gcc-16.2.0
